## 3. Fable 5.1 — narrow auto-ON (hard gates)

Auto-pin Fable **without waiting** only if **all** of A+B+C:

- **A.** Touches: auth/sessions/secrets/encryption · KVKK/GDPR/PII/passenger data · passport/OCR **after failed fix** · irreversible migration / corruption risk · `security-review` · bugbot on those paths · user said `fable`  
- **B.** Task is decision/design/review/correctness-critical edit — not explore/browser/video/log-only  
- **C.** §5 caps allow another Fable Task  

| Id | Gate | Pin |
|----|------|-----|
| F1 | Security review | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F2 | Auth / secrets / encryption | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F3 | KVKK / PII / passenger data | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F4 | OCR/passport retry after failed fix | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` |
| F5 | Irreversible migration / corruption | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` |
| F6 | Trust-boundary + residency/tenancy/local-cloud | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` |
| F7 | Bugbot on F2–F5 paths | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F8 | User said `fable` | named tier or `thinking-high` |
| F9 | Same gate failed on Opus/Sol-xhigh | escalate **one** step once |

**Not Fable:** generic architecture/UI; first-pass OCR (I4); quality words alone; explore/CI/browser/video/docs.

**Pairing:** E1 Composer → one Fable/Opus synthesis → Sol impl. Browser/video = B1/V1.

**Blocked:** fable→Opus-max chain→Sol-max; log it. **Cost-down:** keep F1–F5/F7; soften F6/F9.

---

## 4. Bias (max ±1 unless named)

| Signal | Effect |
|--------|--------|
| Quality words | +1 tier same lane; does **not** alone open Fable |
| Cost/speed | E0/Terra/medium OK; **keep** F1–F5 |
| Named model | That slug; F1–F5 still win on sensitive Tasks |
| Silence | §2 defaults + §0 if parent opaque |

---

## 5. Hard caps (anti-bloat)

Per **user turn:** Fable ≤2 · frontier synthesizers (Fable/Opus-xhigh+/Sol-xhigh+) ≤3 · explore ≤4 Composer-only · `max` only F5/F9 or user-max · `*-fast` on F-gates = 0.

One F9 escalate per problem, then stop/ask/ship.

---

## 6. Model log (mandatory — no opaque-only)

```markdown
### Model log
| # | Operation | Model | Why |
|---|-----------|-------|-----|
| 0 | parent | `cursor-grok-4.6-high` **or** `orchestrator-only (Auto)` | P1 / §0 |
| 1 | … | `exact-slug` | lane E1 / gate F3 / user … |
```

Rules:

- Parent row: explicit slug **or** `orchestrator-only (Auto)` — **never** `routed id hidden` as the story.  
- If parent is orchestrator-only, **≥1 Task row** required whenever work exceeded tiny Q&A.  
- One row per Task; Shell/Edit alone → still need Task for I2+ work planned next, or do I1 via Task when opaque.  
- `Why`: lane/gate/user ≤12 words. Fallbacks: `requested → actual`.  
- Never omit. Inline launch OK: `Pin: composer-2.5 · E1`.

---

## 7. Fallbacks

Same family first: Fable→Opus-max… · Sol→Terra · Grok→medium · Sonnet→medium · Composer→Terra · Gemini→Sonnet · Muse→Composer.  
Hard last resort: Opus ↔ Sol ↔ Grok. No fast/none/low on F-gates.

---

## 8. Anti-patterns

- Doing I2+/R/B/V/F work on opaque Auto parent alone  
- `inherit` under Auto/default  
- Writing `routed id hidden` and stopping  
- Skipping Model log or Task `model`  
- Fable from quality words alone · frontier explore swarms · Fable browser/video  
- Gemini/Muse as backend impl · skipping F1–F5 for cost  

